course: dictionary
lesson: 336
title: One word, two meanings: Anna
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The same word can mean different things. The clues around it tell you which meaning to use. «Tom has 8 apples and Anna gives him 5 more: 8 + 5 = 13, so Tom has 13 apples now.» Anna is a person here, because she gives Tom apples.
explain: Names start with a capital letter. «Anna of Kyiv became Queen of France» uses a capital A because Anna is a name for a girl or woman. Anna is also an old word for a coin of India, and sixteen annas made one rupee.
explain: Ask yourself: does this fit in the sentence? Try the meaning you think of and read the sentence again. If you are reading an old book about India and prices are given in annas and rupees, the word means a coin. If a girl is doing something, the word is a name.
fact: Anna is a girl's name, and it is common in English and in many other languages.
fact: An anna was an old coin of India and nearby lands.
fact: Sixteen annas made one rupee.
fact: Names begin with a capital letter, so «Anna» is written with a capital A.
fact: Old books about India, such as Kipling's, give prices in annas and rupees, which are no longer used as coins in that form.
exercise: «Tom has 8 apples and Anna gives him 5 more.» What is Anna in this sentence? | A kind of apple | *A girl's name | A coin | A town
exercise: In old books about India, how many annas made one rupee? | *Sixteen | Eight | Ten | Twelve
exercise: Why does «Anna» start with a capital letter in «Anna of Kyiv became Queen of France»? | It is a place | It is a very old word | It is a coin | *It is a name, and names start with a capital letter
test: «Anna Yaroslavna became Queen of France in 1051.» What is Anna in this sentence? | A coin | A ship | A rupee | *A person's name
test: What was an anna? | A sort of petrol station | A kind of tea | *An old coin of India and nearby lands | A name for a girl only
exam: Which statement about the word anna is true? | It is a kind of bird | *It can be a girl's name, and it was also an old coin of India | It is always a kind of food | It means very fast
